Presented for your consideration: 
Stupid Ascension Trick 34.2.4 Ascension Post-
Ascended will all artifact weapons.

Some comments:
Going for this SAT meant that I would have to wish for 
at least three artifacts. Of the four classes with a quest artifact
that was a weapon, I chose Samurai because they can get to skilled
in Clerical spells and I knew that I would be casting quite a few
Create Monster spells before the game was over. In retrospect, Healer
might be the better class for this as they start out as Neutral (giving
easy access to all alignments with a HoOA) and they have an altar in
the Quest (so offerings can be done forever).

My plan was to get to the Castle without ever getting artifacts
generated (so no Quest first, no dipping, no offering) and wish for
the three other quest artifact weapons. If I had not been able to get
the three with the Castle Wand, I probably would have abandonded the
game.

After the Castle, the plan was to get all of the non-quest lawfuls by
creating monsters and offering, then get the Tsurugi of Muramasa from
the quest, then convert to Neutral and get the rest of them with more
offering and a Helm of Opposite Alignment as necessary.


In my actual game,  I was lucky in that I got an early extra wish from
a lamp, and the third wish for an artifact was successful. With unused
wishes available from the Castle Wand, I also went for the Eye of the
Aethiopica. It sure saved turns waiting for Power to recharge, and it's
level-porting let return to previously-visited levels of the Quest even
after I changed alignment to Neutral so I was able to leave the Tsurugi
until the very last.

