ascending to Earth. Once there (and killing the Wizard again) I picked
all my stuff up and continued on my own as only walking is required for
the rest of the game, no more stair-climbing. (So, yes, I was going
across the Plane of Air while Stressed. That is a first for me, and I
suppose a bit of a Stupid Trick in its own right, but when you have over
2000 HP, Air Elementals aren't that much of a threat.)

Once on the Astral I headed for Death. I dropped him and then started
reading scrolls of create monster while confused to fill the level with
acid blobs. Once that was done, I waited and watched for the "less
hassled" message. I got it and so no more Death.

Pestilence managed to kill me three times because I wasn't paying enough
attention, was burdened (and so slow), and satiated (and so didn't see
Ill messages). Thankfully I had enough amulets of life saving and eventually
got myself straighted out. After that I started using the Staff of 
Aesculapius on him and dropped him to level 10. I then cast Charm Monster
and had me a pet Rider that really started clean out the level. Famine
I successfully tamed at level 22 or so.

Let me tell you, the Riders make some awesome pets. They quickly worked
their way back up to level 36 and 360 HP or so. They are quite deadly
and even if they are killed (as they were a few times after they started
helping me) they come right back (and stayed tame).

I spent quite a few turns pushing boulders in to surround the Neutral
altar. I wanted to have just 9 spaces so I could arrange a parting
message in pets by displacing them and not have them shifting on me.
The boulders that were not in a position to be pushed I teleported
around until they were in a good spot. That took quite a while.

Finally, I had my arrangement. I had two pet riders, an Archon, a Olog-hai,
two Liches, and all I needed was a G to be able to spell out GOT ALL.
I used cursed genocide to get Gnome Kings, killed all but one and Charmed
that one. Then I stood on the altar and whistled them all in. Some bumping
and displacing and the message takes shape. Finally it is time to offer
the amulet and end this game.
Hmmm... how _will_ I spend my lunch hours now?

